l Disturbance Syndrome with Possible Neuro-ophthalmologic or Vascular Aetiology: contradicted by systemic findings"], "alarm_features": ["1-month weight loss", "35% blasts in peripheral blood", "Pancytopenia (Hb 10 g/dL, Hematocrit 31%, Platelets 109,000/mm³)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3776861408156309, "posterior": 0.12444332265028914, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The combination of 35% blasts and pancytopenia is pathognomonic for myeloid malignancy. This finding strongly supports myeloid neoplasm over other categories."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2072148728143921, "posterior": 0.8755556210109751, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and blasts provide moderate support for lymphoid neoplasm, though absence of lymphocytosis reduces this likelihood compared to myeloid …"], "evidence_against": ["No specific findings directly contradict the myeloid neoplasm hypothesis. Constitutional symptoms and blasts are consistent with myeloid malignancies like AML …"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Plasma Cell Disorder with Pancytopenia", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No specific findings directly contradict the myeloid neoplasm hypothesis. Constitutional symptoms and blasts are consistent with myeloid malignancies like AML …"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis with Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No specific findings directly contradict the myeloid neoplasm hypothesis. Constitutional symptoms and blasts are consistent with myeloid malignancies like AML …"]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal serum calcium level (10.0 mEq/L) rule out multiple myeloma as the cause of pancytopenia and blasts?", "summary": "Hypercalcemia occurs in ~70% of multiple myeloma cases. Normal calcium strongly excludes a plasma cell disorder as the primary cause."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does 35% blasts in peripheral blood with pancytopenia (Hb 10 g/dL, platelets 109k) confidently exclude a non-malignant cause of leukocytosis?", "summary": "35% blasts with pancytopenia are pathognomonic for malignancy. Non-malignant reactive causes are confidently excluded."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset with constitutional symptoms and 35% blasts in peripheral blood with pancytopenia support a myeloid neoplasm (e.g., AML or CML in blast crisis)?", "summary": "The combination of 35% blasts and pancytopenia is pathognomonic for myeloid malignancy. This finding strongly supports myeloid neoplasm over other categories."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms (fever, weight los